I guess it depends on how complex of a solution you need? I recently started just definining colors at the beginning of my markdown scripts by just creating a vector of the colors I want. So just something like:

colors_i_want <- c("red", "blue", "green", "orange")

then later on I just add

scale_fill_manual(values = colors_i_want)

Someone will likely give you a more sophisticated answer but if that's all you need I see no reason to make it more complicated. If you know you're using scale_fill_manual over and over, you could even save that into the object :)

