Hi

It does not seem that there is indeed a simple and clean solution. Building on John, one solution is to redefine scale_colour_discrete based on your choice. Note you need to redefine it for each scale you are likely to use (fill, colour, in discrete and continuous versions)

library(ggplot2)
qplot(data=iris, Petal.Length, Petal.Width, color=Species, size=I(4))

colors_i_want <- c("yellow", "pink", "green", "orange")
scale_colour_discrete <- function(...) scale_colour_manual(..., values = colors_i_want)
scale_fill_discrete <- function(...) scale_fill_manual(..., values = colors_i_want)

last_plot()

